# local-only working files
# Audit notes, agent context, and the pre-prod seed scripts. These were ignored
# only via .git/info/exclude, which git does not track, so the rule protected
# this machine and nothing else — a clone that regenerated these files would
# have swept security reviews and seed scripts into a public repo on the next
# `git add -A`. Kept here so the rule travels with the repo.
#
# Published README assets deliberately live in .github/screenshots/, not under
# docs/, so this stays a plain directory ignore. Do not move them back and add
# a negation: git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded,
# so `/docs/` + `!/docs/screenshots/` silently ignores the negation and the
# README ends up linking images that were never committed.
/docs/
/context/
/scripts/
CLAUDE.md

# verification screenshots
# Every audit cycle leaves browser shots in the repo root, and they pile up
# until someone sweeps them by hand. Root-level only — `public/` images and
# anything nested are untouched.
/*.png